;;; A rule's `:assert (not ?g)` with `?g` bound by a fact only a commitment states: every state past root stores the negation of a guest —
;;; M1f **W84**, register row `W84/not-name-under-commitment`, filed by S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests and a declared relation `seen`, of which no fact is written and which
;;; the hypotheses are taken from, `(solve :hypothesis-relations (seen))`, and a rule
;;; that concludes `(not ?g)` of whoever is seen.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A commitment states `(seen Ann)` or `(seen Bob)`, a fact of a declared relation
;;; over the program's names, so `(seen ?g)` binds `?g` to a name in every state past
;;; root: refused at load, one line, on every command.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: the program loads; H is `(seen Ann)` and `(seen Bob)` and R is
;;; four states, of which three store `(not Ann)`, `(not Bob)` or both. Their
;;; `--dump-answer` state files do not reload. Exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(relation seen Guest :why "{?1} was seen")
(rule deny () :match (seen ?g) :assert (not ?g) :why "not {?g}: they were seen")
(solve :hypothesis-relations (seen))
(query :goal (seen ?g))
